{"kind":"report","text":"READY-FOR-REVIEW at exact head 5caf6e853d838e0a18a47a37a68f7deba6abc3c0 on request/merge-driven-succession, pushed. Primary artifact 436d9587 at cmd/gs; live candidates 7305c1ad at internal/workroom, 9c1c18c8 at internal/docset, 3dc87363 at docs, 465b975e at internal/app. All five are effective, live and not stale, and rest on the request. Main at f8ce4892 is merged into the branch, so the head merges cleanly.\n\nAll three blocking findings of ratified review #4842 are closed, and every one was proved by disabling the fix and watching a named test go red.\n\nFINDING A, the structural citation deadlock. The pages cite exactly the artifacts a merge must retire, so refusing every cited retirement refused every documented-area merge, and the guard's advice to repoint first was unsatisfiable because the successor does not exist until the merge lands. The fix separates the two cases rather than hard-coding either answer. preflightSuccession now refuses only a bare retirement — one whose plan entry names no successor — and refuses a plan naming a successor path it does not itself publish; a retirement the same merge succeeds goes through, because the supersession names the successor artifact standing at that path. The other half is in the documentation gate, which is where the redness would otherwise land: ClassifyCitation takes whether the retirement named a successor, and reports a citation of a retired-with-successor artifact as a flare instead of failing the set, while a retirement that names nothing stays fatal. SucceededRetirements derives that fact from the projection — an effective supersession resting on an artifact at the same path or at a directory covering it. So a merge in a documented area lands, the pages it moves flare and are told where to re-anchor, and re-anchoring is ordinary follow-up work rather than a precondition that cannot be met.\n\nFINDING C, receipt authority. The receipt constrained the approval chain it cited but nothing about its own signer, and merge_head and merge_retirements were signer-chosen strings, so any participant could copy a public ratified approval into an assert of their own and retire a stranger's pointer. Two bounds, both checkable from the log alone. validateMergeReceiptNow requires the receipt to be signed by the author of the implementation artifact the approval covers: the merger of an approved head is the actor whose work it is, so a copied approval carries no plan at all. hasAuthorizedMergeReceipt requires every target to carry a successor path in the signed plan, that path to cover the target's own path, and the supersession to cite the successor artifact published there — so a receipt reaches exactly the tree its merge republished. A bare retirement has no successor to bound the claim and therefore takes no cross-author authority from a merge; a deleted path stays with the target's author or a ratifier, which is what the free-standing rule already said.\n\nFINDING B, the wider-path fixture. The root cause was widest() seeding the winner with the changed path itself, so a narrow artifact at exactly that path was accepted by the fallback arm and the comparison never ran. The seed is now emptiness, with the fallback returned only when nothing covers the change, and the fixture puts both artifacts above the changed file — internal/workroom and internal — in both orders.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE, all run at this head. Dropping the receipt-author binding makes TestMergeReceiptFromABystanderAuthorizesNothing fail with exactly the verdict the review reported: effective, \"merge approval authorized artifact succession\". Dropping the successor-coverage bound fails TestMergeReceiptReachesOnlyWhatItsSuccessorCovers and TestMergeReceiptTakesNoAuthorityOverABareRetirement. Replacing widerPath with `return false` fails TestMergeWiderPathWinsOverNestedArtifact in the first order it tries, where before it changed nothing in the whole package. Restoring the hard-coded refusal fails TestMergeLandsWhenTheCitedPredecessorGetsASuccessor and TestMergePreflightSeparatesSucceededRetirementFromOrphaning, with the original deadlock error text. Passing every citation through as allowed instead fails TestMergeBareRetirementOfACitedPredecessorLeavesTargetUnchanged and the bare arm of the preflight test — so neither the refusal nor the bypass passes. Making any retirement fatal again in the documentation gate fails the retired-with-successor row of TestClassifyCitationSeparatesFatalFromReported.\n\nALSO. planSuccession's merge-head parameter and publishedByThisMerge are removed with the retry test that guarded a path the command could not take; the sealed Git plan is what covers retry and its test is untouched. readMergeReceipt now returns \"not one of ours\" for a commit that is not a complete receipt, so replaying an old approval reports already-used rather than malformed. errorsNewMalformedDiff is a plain error value, mergeReceiptPlan has one lookup instead of three, and staleness() reads the plan once per record rather than once per basis. architecture.md no longer calls the receipt deterministic cross-author succession, gs/merge.md lists the five facts the fold checks and says to restart residents at the merged commit for state@1 and fold@3, and anchoring.md says what makes a retirement survivable for the pages that cited it.\n\nPRESERVED AND STILL GREEN: pre-HEAD-move failure atomicity (TestMergeBareRetirementOfACitedPredecessorLeavesTargetUnchanged carries it, HEAD unmoved and no receipt reservation left), the sealed retry plan, the state@1 admission rule and state@0 evasion closure, exact-head approval binding, and TestMergeLeavesAnUnrelatedCandidateArtifactLive.\n\nGATES at this exact head, in a clean worktree: go vet ./... clean; go build ./... clean; go test ./... -count=1 fully green — 24 packages run together and internal/docset run alone at 330s after waiting for another actor's docset run to finish, since the examples share a fixed port. No ui/ file changed, so no tsc or UI suite was run.\n\nNot merged, as asked. The candidates at 91990a26 belong to another actor and are left live.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:436d958714a50f887f4394b178ae422863754a10","head":"5caf6e853d838e0a18a47a37a68f7deba6abc3c0","status":"ready-for-review"}}